# .dockerignore - what never enters the Docker build context.
#
# Lives at the repository root because Docker resolves it against the build
# context, and `docker/docker-compose.yml` sets that context to the root
# (see `CLAUDE.md` -> Root files, `docker/README.md`).
#
# This is not a copy of `.gitignore`. That file answers "what must never be
# committed"; this one answers "what must never reach the image". The two
# overlap on secrets and build output and diverge everywhere else: the method
# and documentation trees are committed on purpose and have no business in a
# build context, while `.env` is git-ignored yet was still being baked into
# the shipped image.
#
# `docker/Dockerfile` build stage runs `COPY . .`, so everything not listed
# here is copied, and `next build` copies the root `.env` into
# `.next/standalone` (Next copies `.env` and `.env.production` verbatim into
# the standalone output). The runtime stage then copies that standalone
# directory into the distributed image. Excluding `.env` here is what breaks
# that chain: the file never reaches the build stage, so there is nothing for
# Next to copy.
#
# Before adding a line, check what each Dockerfile stage consumes. The build
# stage runs the real Next build, and the runtime stage reads
# `docker/entrypoint.sh` from this context. Excluding something the build
# needs trades a secrets leak for a broken build, which is worse.

# --- Secrets - the reason this file exists (see AD-014) -----------------------
# Real values, never distributed. `.env.example` is re-included below: it is
# the documented template and must stay available.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
# .npmrc can carry a registry token. Nothing needs it: the deps stage installs
# from `package.json` and `pnpm-lock.yaml` only.
.npmrc
**/.npmrc
# Keys and certificates.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx

# --- Local data - the database lives in a volume, never in an image ----------
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
backups/

# --- Build output and dependencies -------------------------------------------
# node_modules is installed in the deps stage and copied from it; a host
# node_modules would be both stale and the wrong platform.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
# A stale .next from a host build, including the standalone output that
# carries the leaked .env.
.next
out
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache

# --- Version control ----------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Method, specification and documentation trees ----------------------------
# Prose, not application code. Nothing in any stage reads them.
# `docker/` is deliberately absent from this list: the runtime stage runs
# `COPY docker/entrypoint.sh`, which reads from this context.
ai-rules
ai-agents
specs
design
context
.devcontainer
.claude
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
# LICENSE stays in the context on purpose: the project ships as a distributed
# image and the license travels with it.

# --- Tests --------------------------------------------------------------------
# The image runs the application; it never runs the suites.
tests
e2e
playwright.config.ts
vitest.config.mts
vitest.setup.ts
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
.playwright

# --- Logs, OS and editor noise ------------------------------------------------
*.log
**/*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea
.vscode
